{"authored" [{"question" "q-35836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{24{x}^{3}-1}{2c{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}}$ is $y=-\\frac{1}{3},$ find the value of $c.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "07573658eff130d94c5313ba5ea3552655c3f9092450b25ddd159d6220deebdb" "basis" 1959 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{24{x}^{3}-1}{2c{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{24{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2c{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(24-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(2c-\\frac{15}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-0}{2c-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{c} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ c & =-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "07573658eff130d94c5313ba5ea3552655c3f9092450b25ddd159d6220deebdb" "basis" 1959 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "676328569b5bb4acd4e792fd6c7af932391b625915f768e9cf989243045eaf29" "basis" 1959 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "07573658eff130d94c5313ba5ea3552655c3f9092450b25ddd159d6220deebdb" "basis" 1959 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-36"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "07573658eff130d94c5313ba5ea3552655c3f9092450b25ddd159d6220deebdb" "basis" 1959 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "07573658eff130d94c5313ba5ea3552655c3f9092450b25ddd159d6220deebdb" "basis" 1959 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questi