 "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{24{x}^{3}-1}{2c{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{24{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2c{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(24-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(2c-\\frac{15}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-0}{2c-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{c} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ c & =-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a12096137ad8dc1d1ddfcf9f4f8a2df471c0c1c2c2df5ad2b548ca3a5e253d3"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-36"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-35836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-36"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $H=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${H}^{3}.$\n\n| ${H}^{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to find ${H}^{2},$ we multiply $H$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{2} & =H\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}23 & -18 \\\\ 9 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${H}^{3}={H}^{2}\\cdot H,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{3} & ={H}^{2}\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}23 & -18 \\\\ 9 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}97 & -118 \\\\ 59 & 38\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a12096137ad8dc1d1ddfcf9f4f8a2df471c0c1c2c2df5ad2b548ca3a5e253d3"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "97"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-118"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "59"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-279424" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "38"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=7+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =7+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{3}{7})=(-25.376\\,933…)^{∘}≈-{25.377}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{25.377}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={334.623}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}={334.623}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/assets/2358d2c829f52ba8727afc10a609f923ca441bb55dc398cda78c619454f6eac5.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{25.377}^{∘} \\\\  & ={205.377}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈{205}^{∘},\\,x≈{335}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a12096137ad8dc1d1ddfcf9f4f8a2df471c0c1c2c2df5ad2b548ca3a5e253d3"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "205"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-338763" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "335"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-342050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-342050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-5{y}^{-1}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5(-{y}^{-2})+2y \\\\  & =2y+5{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{5}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{3}+5}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}+5}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2(1)^{3}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (x-(-4)) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{4}{7}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{11}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-342050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a12096137ad8dc1d1ddfcf9f4f8a2df471c0c1c2c2df5ad2b548ca3a5e253d3"} {"question" "q-342050" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-342050" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+11}{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-135990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${(1-5t)}^{7}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-135990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-5t$ and $n=7$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-5t)}^{7} & =1+7\\cdot (-5t)+\\frac{7(7-1)}{2!}\\cdot (-5t)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-35t+\\frac{7\\cdot 6}{2}\\cdot 25{t}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-35t+21\\cdot 25{t}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-35t+525{t}^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-135990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a12096137ad8dc1d1ddfcf9f4f8a2df471c0c1c2c2df5ad2b548ca3a5e253d3"} {"question" "q-135990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-135990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+25t+450{t}^{2}+⋯"] ["math" "1+35t+485{t}^{2}+⋯"] ["math" "1-21t+550{t}^{2}+⋯"] ["math" "1-35t+500{t}^{2}+⋯"] ["math" "1-35t+525{t}^{2}+⋯"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/state.json" "file_sha256" "256cda91cc320f4a79f94ce24e464377be6d65d22d5e189ebc42986c1f85b82c"} {"question" "q-135990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-35t+525{t}^{2}+⋯"] "category" "ma_successful